+# MUWEB R90 FIX95 — CharacterHelper table/render/routing closure
+
+Parent: **FIX94**. Status: **DEVELOPMENT / NOT PROMOTED**.
+
+## Why this was a large port
+
+The current client's `CharacterHelper.lua` is table-driven. Its 2.4 MB source defines `HELPER_CONFIG = {...}` and only later loops over that table to invoke `SetHelper`. The old Web parser looked primarily for literal `SetHelper(GET_ITEM(...), ...)` calls. On the consolidated current-client layout that can yield zero helper owners even though all data is present.
+
+FIX95 reads the authored table itself and keeps the existing single loader/registry. It does not create a second helper manager.
+
+## Current-client audit
+
+The supplied `CharacterHelper.lua` produced:
+
+- **204** helper config rows;
+- raw type distribution: **83 Type0**, **3 Type2**, **55 Type3**, **61 Type4**, **2 Type5**;
+- **155** `RENDER_HELPER[ItemID]` owners;
+- **1,208** model/render rows;
+- **647** plain `RENDER_TEXTURE` rows;
+- **561** additional fixed-function passes;
+- **143** helper-level shadow owners;
+- **155** FootEffect blocks.
+
+These counts are an audit of the supplied Lua source, not hard-coded runtime content. Runtime still reads the official client's Data.
+
+## Model ownership
+
+PC `HelperSystem/OpenItems` semantics are retained:
+
+- `Model` is the inventory/item BMD, normally under `Data\Item\`;
+- `ObjectModel` is the creature BMD for Type>0, normally under `Data\Skill\`;
+- Type0 renders its item model directly;
+- Type>0 receives the ObjectModel/synthetic model identity;
+- explicit `ModelDir` and `ObjectModelDir` from the Lua are preserved.
+
+This prevents the previous class of errors where a flying pet's icon/item BMD could be used as the creature model, or a mount/helper could be routed to the wrong family.
+
+## RENDER_HELPER presentation
+
+`PcCharacterHelperPresentation.js` consumes deterministic model passes from the real Lua table.
+
+- `Glow=2 / RENDER_TEXTURE / Texture=-1` uses the already resident BMD mesh, avoiding duplicate base draws.
+- Other authored flags create an overlay on the same geometry/skeleton.
+- RGB, mesh index, repetition Value, numeric texture override and authored dynamic UV/color formulas are retained where they are representable 1:1.
+- unsupported texture IDs, dynamic chance/timer branches, native shadow projection and foot-effect lifecycle are recorded fail-closed rather than replaced by generic graphics.
+
+## Category routing
+
+The Lua `RenderHelper` dispatcher proves separate domains. FIX95 stops treating every custom helper as a flying helper:
+
+- raw Type0 -> flying/helper lane;
+- raw Type3 -> custom Fenrir behavior lane;
+- raw Type4 -> custom Horse/DarkHorse behavior lane;
+- raw Type2 and Type5 -> explicit unresolved movement owner for now.
+
+This routing is propagated to hero equipment, Character Select, F3:72 elements and other players in the viewport. The viewport also materializes stock/custom rider companions, which previously could be visible on the local hero but absent on remote players.
+
+## Explicit remaining debt
+
+- `RenderShadowModel`: needs the exact native projection/terrain owner; no fake blob shadow.
+- FootEffect: requires exact Horse/Fenrir/other helper effect lifecycle per family.
+- Type2 Dinorant and Type5 Dragon movement/action semantics.
+- CharacterSetEffect `CreateSkill` second `CreateEffect` child for IDs without proven lifecycle.
+- CustomCape global effect/joint/shadow families.
+- Remaining map/material/skill/event and physical performance validation.
+
+## Validation gates
+
+FIX95 includes gates for:
+
+- HELPER_CONFIG parsing and Item/Skill ownership;
+- RENDER_HELPER parser/owner;
+- helper category routing;
+- helper presentation structural behavior;
+- inherited FIX45 helper/Lua gate;
+- FIX93 Fenrir Foot Thunder gate;
+- FIX94 large-port gate;
+- whole-tree JS/MJS/CJS syntax;
+- immutable source hash verification.
